<Defs>

  <!--
    The shapes the gods take on the map (ColonyCouncil.GodShapeDef; Source/ColonyCouncil/Gods/OnMap/GodShapes.cs). The
    player: "not every god necessarily has to have a sacred beast, each god should be individual in what it looks like
    and whether it has any form at all". Who comes, and as what, is read from here, never decided by the code:
      stranger: it can come as a lone traveller asking for shelter, in disguise (only the Guest wears human shapes);
      beast, beasts, look, kin, kinCount: it walks as a beast, which (ThingDef names), in which look, and with others of
        its kind following at a distance;
      leads, feeds, sitNear: what the colony can do with its beast (follow it where it leads, take it food, sit near it
        while it grazes); harmIsWorst: harming it or its kin is the worst thing a colony can do;
      weather, voices: it answers in the weather, and with which voices (Rain, Thunder, Eclipse, Aurora, Cold, Snow);
      bodiless: no body on the map at all: it acts through plants, rot, machines, the sky, frost or the dark, and answers
        in the sky more readily;
      omens: its own signs (GodOmens), in place of the five any god may send;
      rises: very rarely it rises from the land for an hour, with no body of its own (Hollin);
      lineTag: the tag its own lines carry.
    The nine are named by their short name in gods (docs/gods-pantheon-brainstorm.md, "The nine"). The shapes by domain
    after them are the fallback only, for a god with no shape of its own.
  -->

  <!-- ===================== The nine ===================== -->

  <!-- Hollin, the Rootmother: the web of roots under the world. Seen in the plants, the anima trees and her dryads; once in a long while she rises. -->
  <ColonyCouncil.GodShapeDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_GodShape_Hollin</defName>
    <gods><li>Hollin</li><li>Rimfolk_God_Hollin</li></gods>
    <stranger>false</stranger>
    <beast>false</beast>
    <bodiless>true</bodiless>
    <rises>true</rises>
    <voices><li>Rain</li></voices>
    <omens><li>Drift</li><li>AnimaHum</li><li>DryadsStill</li></omens>
    <lineTag>hollin</lineTag>
  </ColonyCouncil.GodShapeDef>

  <!--
    Smoulder, the Coil Under the Mountain: a dragon asleep in the rock. He never comes on the map: his shadow at noon,
    his breath in the steam, his turning in the deep mines. A colony that mines past every warning wakes him (GodWaking):
    the deep working closes, and where the gods walk plainly his true form comes up out of the mountain for a few hours,
    Dragon's Descent's true dragon (by name, when the mod is loaded), red and black.
  -->
  <ColonyCouncil.GodShapeDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_GodShape_Smoulder</defName>
    <gods><li>Smoulder</li><li>Rimfolk_God_Smoulder</li></gods>
    <stranger>false</stranger>
    <beast>false</beast>
    <bodiless>true</bodiless>
    <weather>false</weather>
    <omens><li>Shadow</li><li>Steam</li><li>Rumble</li></omens>
    <lineTag>smoulder</lineTag>
    <trueForm>True_Dragon</trueForm>
    <trueLook>Rimfolk_GodLook_Smoulder</trueLook>
  </ColonyCouncil.GodShapeDef>

  <!-- Bellwether, the Old Horn: the first thrumbo, white and huge, other thrumbos following at a distance. To be let pass (a strange peace after); someone may sit near him; harming him or his kin is the worst thing. -->
  <ColonyCouncil.GodShapeDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_GodShape_Bellwether</defName>
    <gods><li>Bellwether</li><li>Rimfolk_God_Bellwether</li></gods>
    <stranger>false</stranger>
    <beasts><li>Thrumbo</li></beasts>
    <look>Rimfolk_GodLook_Bellwether</look>
    <kin>Thrumbo</kin>
    <kinCount>1~3</kinCount>
    <leads>false</leads>
    <feeds>false</feeds>
    <sitNear>true</sitNear>
    <harmIsWorst>true</harmIsWorst>
    <peace>true</peace>
    <weather>false</weather>
    <omens><li>Restless</li><li>Calm</li><li>Dream</li></omens>
    <lineTag>bellwether</lineTag>
  </ColonyCouncil.GodShapeDef>

  <!-- Morel, the Soft Mother: alive in every thread of mould and mushroom. Fairy rings, the smell of earth, white threads. -->
  <ColonyCouncil.GodShapeDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_GodShape_Morel</defName>
    <gods><li>Morel</li><li>Rimfolk_God_Morel</li></gods>
    <stranger>false</stranger>
    <beast>false</beast>
    <bodiless>true</bodiless>
    <weather>false</weather>
    <omens><li>FairyRing</li><li>Earth</li><li>Threads</li></omens>
    <lineTag>morel</lineTag>
  </ColonyCouncil.GodShapeDef>

  <!-- Ennu, the Guest: the only one who wears human shapes, as the stranger at the gate. -->
